From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] crypt32: async handles and the Unicode registry/CryptoAPI wrappers

- CryptCreateAsyncHandle, CryptSetAsyncParam, CryptGetAsyncParam and
  CryptCloseAsyncHandle were stubs. A handle now holds parameters named by
  an OID string or an integer; setting a name again frees the old value
  with its function and closing the handle frees all of them.
- The exported Unicode wrappers Reg{Open,Create}KeyExU, Reg{Query,Set}
  ValueExU, RegEnumValueU, RegDeleteValueU, RegQueryInfoKeyU,
  CryptEnumProvidersU, CryptSetProviderU, CryptSignHashU and
  CryptVerifySignatureU were stubs; they forward to the advapi32 wide
  functions like CryptAcquireContextU already does.
---
--- a/dlls/crypt32/Makefile.in
+++ b/dlls/crypt32/Makefile.in
@@ -8,6 +8,7 @@ UNIX_LIBS    = $(SECURITY_LIBS)
 UNIX_CFLAGS  = $(GNUTLS_CFLAGS)
 
 SOURCES = \
+	async.c \
 	base64.c \
 	cert.c \
 	chain.c \
new file mode 100644
--- /dev/null
+++ b/dlls/crypt32/async.c
@@ -0,0 +1,243 @@
+/*
+ * crypt32 async handles: named parameters a caller attaches to an
+ * asynchronous retrieval and that are freed when the handle is closed.
+ *
+ * Copyright 2026 Stained Glass OS
+ *
